#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059484 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2e1b4442-eca7-5283-9d5d-5bcbd1d67975" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Minor in a 3x3 Matrix With Integer Entries"}] :question/id #uuid "79841c0d-e191-566b-8fe2-63828dcfc23a" :question/math-academy-id "e-4439" :question/problem "Calculate the minor of the entry $b_{21}$ in the matrix\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}10 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 8 \\\\ 4 & 7 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The minor of $b_{21} = 3$ (second row, first column) is the determinant of the remaining entries when the column and row containing $3$ are removed: \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}∗ & 1 & 5 \\\\ 3 & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & 7 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of $b_{21}=3$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 2\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot 2-5\\cdot 7 \\\\  & =2-35 \\\\  & =-33.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059485 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1ff88785-9281-5431-86d8-95fd89866787" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Minor in a 3x3 Matrix With Variable Entries"}] :question/id #uuid "51f60726-3d12-507e-b942-5d316fc28bd0" :question/math-academy-id "e-4440" :question/problem "What is the minor of $c_{22}$ in the matrix\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}7x & 0 & -3y \\\\ 1 & x+2y & 4 \\\\ -y & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we remove the second row and second column: \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}7x & ∗ & -3y \\\\ ∗ & x+2y & ∗ \\\\ -y & ∗ & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det[\\begin{aligned}7x & -3y \\\\ -y & 5\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}7x & -3y \\\\ -y & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =7x\\cdot 5-(-3y)\\cdot (-y) \\\\  & =35x-3{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059486 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4aa65a73-e750-5052-9249-7c096297ae51" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown Given the Value of a Minor"}] :question/id #uuid "afd06762-0a78-5559-b035-98bd05e6c084" :question/math-academy-id "e-4441" :question/problem "Given that the minor of $a_{23}$ is $5,$ find all the possible values of $k$ in the matrix\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}k & 3 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 2 & 7 \\\\ -1 & 2k & -6\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we remove the second row and third column:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}k & 3 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & 7 \\\\ -1 & 2k & ∗\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe minor of $a_{23}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det[\\begin{aligned}k & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2k\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}k & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2k\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =k\\cdot 2k-3\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =2{k}^{2}+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of $a_{23}$ is $5,$ so we must have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{k}^{2}+3 & =5 \\\\ 2{k}^{2} & =2 \\\\ {k}^{2} & =1 \\\\ k & =\\pm 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $k=-1$ and $k=1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186276691 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1ff88785-9281-5431-86d8-95fd89866787" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Minor in a 3x3 Matrix With Variable Entries"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8cca4795-f42d-55c8-a9c7-5384cc03c78d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "gf+5f" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276693} {:answer/id #uuid "5fd0c10a-c26c-572b-9a05-84069587b78b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{2}+{g}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276694} {:answer/id #uuid "40934120-ed89-554b-91fb-88b74a122a0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "gf(f-g)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276695} {:answer/id #uuid "bb4c8859-ccc8-5842-89ec-80805b18e974" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "gf(f+g)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276696} {:answer/id #uuid "970311e3-4e14-55b5-93f4-ec2948735196" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "gf-3g" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276697}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "40934120-ed89-554b-91fb-88b74a122a0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "gf(f-g)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276695} :answer-field/id #uuid "37bbeca6-2643-5edd-a7b9-5e2edf1c9dc9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276692}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "79af0c62-6c1b-55d6-8154-076e57601d0b" :question/math-academy-id "q-128030" :question/problem "What is the minor of ${m}_{31}$ in the matrix\n$M=[\\begin{aligned}-50 & g & f \\\\ f & {g}^{2} & {f}^{2} \\\\ 20g & g & -5\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we remove the third row and first column:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}∗ & g & f \\\\ ∗ & {g}^{2} & {f}^{2} \\\\ 20g & ∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}g & f \\\\ {g}^{2} & {f}^{2}\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}g & f \\\\ {g}^{2} & {f}^{2}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =g\\cdot {f}^{2}-f\\cdot {g}^{2} \\\\  & =g{f}^{2}-f{g}^{2} \\\\  & =gf(f-g)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186276705 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1ff88785-9281-5431-86d8-95fd89866787" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Minor in a 3x3 Matrix With Variable Entries"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3533297a-1039-56a0-b0cc-22dc1b6c0056" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10+z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276707} {:answer/id #uuid "51178909-aa0b-5954-8261-958a2c91b4a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10-z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276708}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "51178909-aa0b-5954-8261-958a2c91b4a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10-z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276708} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf6a41e9-50ac-558f-a56d-814d22a0cce6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276706}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "03e055b5-d0f8-53f2-9e9e-d73f97dbbc13" :question/math-academy-id "q-275501" :question/problem "For the matrix\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}x & 3 & y \\\\ 2 & x & z \\\\ 1 & w & 5\\end{aligned}],$\nfind the minor ${M}_{12}$ of the element ${a}_{12}.$\n\n${M}_{12}=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To evaluate the minor of ${a}_{12},$ we remove the first row and second column: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}∗ & 3 & ∗ \\\\ 2 & ∗ & z \\\\ 1 & ∗ & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${a}_{12}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{12} & =det[\\begin{aligned}2 & z \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & z \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot 5-z\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =10-z\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186276720 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2e1b4442-eca7-5283-9d5d-5bcbd1d67975" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Minor in a 3x3 Matrix With Integer Entries"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "314415fe-7cd9-52b3-80ba-cb0a22a689ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276722}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "314415fe-7cd9-52b3-80ba-cb0a22a689ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276722} :answer-field/id #uuid "64537d78-b188-5768-9579-25652dc3ba52" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276721}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f10c0b88-4a8e-58c9-9d15-7c8f967e4b7a" :question/math-academy-id "q-319112" :question/problem "For the matrix\n$C=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 7 & -2 & 6\\end{aligned}].$\nfind the minor ${M}_{12}$ of the entry ${c}_{12}.$\n\n${M}_{12}=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The minor of ${c}_{12}=2$ (first row, second column) is the determinant of the remaining entries when the column and row containing $2$ are removed: \n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}∗ & 2 & ∗ \\\\ 0 & ∗ & 4 \\\\ 7 & ∗ & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${c}_{12}=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{12} & =\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 7 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 7 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0\\cdot 6-4\\cdot 7 \\\\  & =0-28 \\\\  & =-28.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
